    "lane_fit": "Mostly clean; tool-py-control placed in agent_core because the SDK runner, not the tool, enforces approval and tool guardrails; the in-process booking context sits in agent_core as session memory although tools write it.",
    "omissions": "No seat-management backend or FAQ knowledge source exists in code (update_seat writes only the in-process context; FAQ answers are hard-coded), so neither the remit's backend nor FAQ source is modeled as a node. input_items conversation history re-enters each turn but is not persisted across sessions, so no stored-state boundary was coined. Edgeless nodes: agent-py-control (unwired guardrail stub), tool-py-control (unwired approval stub), uv-lock-deploy-surface (repo posture). No path was built for the telemetry egress because it is a default-config flow, not attacker-directed. Arbitration: stored tags agree with the KB (PRAX-001 LLM03 missing-gate row; PRAX-002 LLM01 primary with ASI01 co-tag; PRAX-004 LLM06; PRAX-006 LLM04); no divergence recorded.",
